# Bundled Python sidecar binaries (built per-OS in CI by
# scripts/build_sidecar_binary.py; never committed).
binaries/
# Cargo.lock IS committed, deliberately.
#
# This crate is a binary (the Tauri shell), and Cargo's own guidance is to
# commit the lockfile for binaries — it is libraries that leave it out. Without
# it CI re-resolves every dependency on each run, so the build depends on what
# crates.io published that morning rather than on anything in this repo.
#
# That is not hypothetical: `desktop-shell` was green on 2026-09-21 and red on
# 2026-09-28 with no Rust change in between, because the tauri crates published
# releases requiring rustc 1.90 while CI pins 1.88.0. A committed lockfile
# makes a toolchain bump an explicit, reviewable commit instead of a surprise
# on an unrelated PR.
gen/
.tauri/
